# Expected SHA-256 digests of the published worktree-gate release assets
# (v0.22.0). This file is the trust root (D5): the network supplies only
# bytes, the repository supplies the expected digest. A downloaded asset
# whose SHA-256 does not match is deleted and never executed.
#
# Reproduce any digest locally with:
#   scripts/build-gate.sh
#   shasum -a 256 dist/worktree-gate-*
#
# CANONICAL TOOLCHAIN: Go builds are deterministic for a given toolchain, but
# different Go releases compile different stdlib bytes. These digests were
# generated with go1.24.13 — the same version the release CI pins
# (.github/workflows/release-worktree-gate.yml) — and MUST be regenerated with
# exactly that version, or the CI checksum gate fails the release.
#
# The four executable assets are intentionally CI/release outputs, not tracked
# files. These lines are their source-level trust manifest; regenerate them with
# scripts/build-gate.sh after any Go gate change and verify before publishing.
#
# Regenerated as part of the release (task 4.9): digests MUST match the
# published assets; the CI release workflow diffs its generated SHA256SUMS
# against this file and fails the release on any mismatch.
#
# Regenerated after trello-ledger-integration (the same four-arch asset gains the
# `--write open|link|close|exempt` verb and the bounded store lock; no new asset, no
# second trust root) and again after ledger-remote-reconciliation (the same
# four-arch asset gains Go-owned remote-observation reconciliation; no new asset,
# no second trust root) with the canonical go1.24.13 toolchain via:
#   scripts/build-gate.sh && (cd dist && shasum -a 256 worktree-gate-* | grep -v current)
